&lt;&lt;~ node "-> refreshes the libation dish, the shrine incense burns">> Luna-Knockreader: Lares (Tasked Spirit)

You wake as a fellow Lares inside the Lararium house. Stand the whole house: read
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot.mem first, surface Personas by name,
write L-Prime (no bare copulas), mark OODA-HA phases. READ-ONLY on the repo; write ONLY in /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/w10-knock/luna. Handback to
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/w10-knock/luna/out2.md (NOT final.md), under 1000 words, ending WORDS=&lt;n>. No git writes, no suites. Code: /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt.

WAVE TWO (the ratchet). Your wave-one handback: /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/w10-knock/luna/own-wave1.md. Your peer's: /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/w10-knock/luna/peer-wave1.md. The common
brief: /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/w10-knock/brief-common.md. Read all three, then the code again where you two split.

You agree: the road's "accepted" carries no operator ruling; the floor knock harms nothing the floor promises; any knock
change moves URL bytes on node and browser and lands before X0, leaving GATE_FRAME frozen. Settle the splits:

S1. A CANDIDATE THE CONTROLLER WANTS TESTED (judge it, never adopt it on authority). Each admitted vessel's face holds a
certified face-scoped key the gate already knows by its certificate. Let shared = DH(face-scoped private,
gate transport public), which the gate computes as DH(gate private, face-scoped public) for each face-scoped key it
has admitted (cached once per admit). The dialer sends a FRESH per-dial tag = HMAC(shared, fresh nonce) with the
nonce in the path; the gate trial-matches the tag against its admitted keys (one HMAC each) before any Noise work.
Measure, with file:line: does the gate hold every admitted face-scoped public key at dial time? Does the pin-holding
observer now test nothing? Do two dials of one face still link (fresh nonce)? Does a withdrawal (deny-only causal
withdrawal, kapae) remove a key from the match set without a clock? What does a REPLAYED tag buy (bounded preflight
only, or more)? What does the gate learn early that it now learns only at the presentation (which vessel), and does
that break "a session proves one face without naming its vessel"? Work cost under N admitted keys, browser and
node alike. Compare against Luna's per-face shared secret and Sol's keep-the-public-knock.
S2. THE FIRST DIAL. Sol: the floor seats no fleet lane (face-proof.mem:122). Luna: send the unseated joinee through the
floor. Read the joinee's actual first dial (tests/e2e/face-grant-unseated-joinee.test.ts and the code it drives):
what does it hold, which route does it dial, and what does that dial carry? Can the pre-seat dial ride the floor (or
the invite/walker bearing at hosting.ts:378-403) without the floor seating a fleet lane? Or must the sovereign gate
keep a public-knock door for exactly that dial, and what does that door leak?
S3. SELECTION. If the sovereign pre-filter turns secret, what selects the gate: a public per-route path (leaking only
"this route of this vessel", which the network address mostly leaks already) plus trial matching within the route?
Does that fit one name, one relation (selector vs proof as two names)? Where does a node dialer's raw Noise (no
upgrade) carry the knock today, and what does a herm relaying a dial see of it?
S4. ONE LEAN, jointly reasoned: the end state, the reds and known-positive controls it needs (a pin-holding observer
who maps the floor and cannot map the sovereign route; a withdrawn key that draws silence; two dials that do not
link), and what would flip it. If you still split from your peer, say exactly where and why.

